<article class="env-remark" id="A883EF">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/A883EF">Remark <span data-tag="A883EF">8.1.5.5</span>.</a> Let $\calC $ be a presentable category, $S$ a collection morphisms in $\calC $, and $\{ Y_{\alpha } \} _{\alpha \in A}$ an $S$-tree in $\calC $. Let $B \subseteq A$ be closed downward. For $\alpha \in A - B$, let $B_{\alpha } = B \cup \{  \beta \in A: \beta \leq \alpha \} $, and let $Z_{\alpha } = Y_{B_{\alpha }}$. Then $ \{  Z_{\alpha } \} _{ \alpha \in A-B}$ is an $S$-tree in $\calC $ with root $Y_{B}$. </p>
